From c025f3d8d4ef27ec579879d3f567373e1a415e77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:30:14 -0300
Subject: [RFC PATCH 3/7] libevent22: new package

Pantavisor talks to its cloud over HTTPS through evhttp on an mbed TLS
bufferevent. That backend only exists in libevent 2.2, and 2.2 has only
alpha releases. Bumping libevent would put an alpha under every package
that uses it and change their soname, so add 2.2 as a second package
instead, which only its users link:

 - static libraries only, with position-independent code, and nothing
   installed on the target;
 - installed to a private sysroot prefix, /usr/lib/libevent-2.2, so the
   headers, libevent.so and libevent.pc of libevent 2.1 stay untouched
   and both packages can be enabled at once. Users add that prefix to
   their search paths.

Options as for libevent, plus mbed TLS instead of OpenSSL and an option
for libevent's debug mode. Two patches: a fix for evhttp crashing when
a connection on a TLS bufferevent is freed with callbacks still queued,
and the CMake debug postfix that the autotools .pc files carry by
mistake.

Once 2.2 has a stable release, this package goes and libevent is
bumped.

Signed-off-by: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
